Imagine you are building a secure enterprise application. You write a CloudStorage class that saves user data to the cloud.
Six months later, the boss says: "We need to encrypt the data before saving it."
The junior developer uses extends to create: class EncryptedCloudStorage extends CloudStorage.

A month later, the boss says: "We also need to compress the data to save space."
The junior developer creates: class CompressedCloudStorage extends CloudStorage.

Then the boss says: "Some customers want Encryption AND Compression!"
The junior developer creates: class EncryptedAndCompressedCloudStorage extends CloudStorage.